From 5e39d19d46970facbbd870198be5df31f9ea8db5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 14:32:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] bus: ti-sysc: populate simple-mfd child nodes too

ti-sysc populates the children of an interconnect target module, but
only descends into "simple-bus" nodes. A "syscon", "simple-mfd" node
inside a target module (dt-schema rejects "syscon", "simple-bus" for new
bindings) gets a device, but its own children never do. The OMAP4 SAR
RAM needs this for a syscon-reboot-mode child.

Match "simple-mfd" as well, like of_default_bus_match_table does. No
existing OMAP device tree has a simple-mfd node under a ti-sysc target
module, so nothing else changes.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/bus/ti-sysc.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bus/ti-sysc.c b/drivers/bus/ti-sysc.c
index e118b900c9ac..149c17aff18e 100644
--- a/drivers/bus/ti-sysc.c
+++ b/drivers/bus/ti-sysc.c
@@ -3142,6 +3142,7 @@ static int sysc_check_active_timer(struct sysc *ddata)
 
 static const struct of_device_id sysc_match_table[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "simple-bus", },
+	{ .compatible = "simple-mfd", },
 	{ /* sentinel */ },
 };
 
